  "details": "Installing Terrain Tools does several weird behavious depending on order of importing of packages\nIt causes compile errors* that can be fixed by editing the source (e.g. using an other exception)\nBy fixing it, Project compiles again and lets me build & test without setting the basic VRChat properties (e.g. layers, etc...) (Didnt test \"publish for windows\")\nAlso doing this, there is no option to set those properties\n*error:\nLibrary\\PackageCache\\com.unity.terrain-tools@3.0.2-preview.3\\Editor\\TerrainToolbox\\ToolboxHelper.cs(221,15): error CS0433: The type 'InvalidDataException' exists in both 'AWSSDK.Core, Version=3.3.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null' and 'System, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b77a5c561934e089'\n(I also installed Udonsharp and CyanEmu, but as far as I can tell, they dont have any impact)\nSystem Info Unity Version : Unity2019.4.28f1 SDK Version : U2019-VRCSDK3-WORLD-2021.07.23.18.12",
